# LF everywhere by default.
#
# This repository is shell scripts, Node, Markdown and a generated SVG, all of
# which must be byte-identical on every platform: a CRLF checkout breaks a
# script at its shebang, and it breaks the banner's drift test, which compares
# the committed file against freshly generated bytes. Pinning the default is
# more durable than listing extensions, which is how both of those bugs reached
# CI in the first place.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Spelled out because these two are load-bearing. A CRLF shell script fails with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", which is what a Windows student would
# hit running them under WSL or Git Bash.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf

# The one exception: PowerShell is a Windows artefact and keeps CRLF.
*.ps1     text eol=crlf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
